    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "10.77 avg cores of 32 allowed (S5)"
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 6215 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "unresolved_modifications",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "11 modification(s) could not be mapped to a UNIMOD accession or a mass, and are carried in ProForma as [Info:...] tags: UniProt:(3S)-3-hydroxyasparagine on N, UniProt:(3S)-3-hydroxyhistidine on H, UniProt:3'-nitrotyrosine on Y, UniProt:5-glutamyl histamine on Q, UniProt:5-glutamyl serotonin on Q, UniProt:Lysino-D-alanine (Lys) on K, UniProt:N6-crotonyllysine on K, UniProt:N6-malonyllysine on K, UniProt:N6-succinyllysine on K, UniProt:O-palmitoleoyl serine on S, UniProt:Omega-hydroxyceramide glutamate ester on Q. Their ptm_sites rows exist and carry modification_name, with modification null, so a query by name finds them and a query by UNIMOD accession will not."
   },
   {
    "code": "isobaric_reference_channels",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "108 channel(s) of the search's TmtDesign.txt are not study samples: `Sample Type` empty: `PXD057861:20230410_GH_Retina_TMT-10_16plex_rep1:TMT134C`, `PXD057861:20230410_GH_Retina_TMT-10_16plex_rep1:TMT135N`, `PXD057861:20230410_GH_Retina_TMT-10_16plex_rep2:TMT134C`, `PXD057861:20230410_GH_Retina_TMT-10_16plex_rep2:TMT135N`, `PXD057861:20230410_GH_Retina_TMT-10_16plex_rep3:TMT134C` and 103 more. Their values measure that reference, not a sample of the question. The design is copied in `sources/`."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_ingested",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "PTM site occupancy was not stored: this is a TMT dataset, and MetaMorpheus computes intensity occupancy for label-free searches only; its count occupancy is per file, repeated on every channel (QuantProject DEF-OCC-INT). `ptm_stoichiometry` has no rows here because of that, not because no site was modified."
   }
